invariant: INV-7
file: suite.h
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: the AES-first default order puts AES-128-GCM ahead of AES-256-GCM,
  where docs/decisions.md 80 puts AES-256-GCM first for CNSA 2.0, which
  requires AES-256 and SHA-384. The hello's cipher_suites bytes must list
  AES-256-GCM first.

--- old
    SUITE_AES_256_GCM_SHA384, SUITE_AES_128_GCM_SHA256, SUITE_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256};
--- new
    SUITE_AES_128_GCM_SHA256, SUITE_AES_256_GCM_SHA384, SUITE_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256};
